Input: {"question": "Who is the artist of the main song in the \"Footloose\" soundtrack?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0266-37edbbfd3395:d00", "start": 0, "end": 107, "text": "he had four stunt doubles: \"I had a stunt double, a dance double [Peter Tramm] and two gymnastics doubles.\""}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0266-37edbbfd3395:d00", "start": 108, "end": 184, "text": "The soundtrack was released in cassette, 8-track tape, vinyl, and CD format."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0266-37edbbfd3395:d00", "start": 185, "end": 272, "text": "The soundtrack was also re-released on CD for the 15th anniversary of the film in 1999."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0266-37edbbfd3395:d00", "start": 273, "end": 494, "text": "The re-release included four new songs: \"Bang Your Head (Metal Health)\" by Quiet Riot, \"Hurts So Good\" by John Mellencamp, \"Waiting for a Girl Like You\" by Foreigner, and the extended 12\" remix of \"Dancing in the Sheets\"."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0266-37edbbfd3395:d00", "start": 495, "end": 583, "text": "The album includes \"Footloose\" and \"I'm Free\", both by Kenny Loggins, \"Holding Out for a"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0266-37edbbfd3395:d01", "start": 0, "end": 25, "text": "Ross Produced by Lewis J."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0266-37edbbfd3395:d01", "start": 26, "end": 524, "text": "Rachmil Craig Zadan Written by Dean Pitchford Starring Kevin Bacon Lori Singer Dianne Wiest John Lithgow Music by Tom Snow Jim Steinman Taylor Swift Dean Pitchford Cinematography by Ric Waite Edited by Paul Hirsch Studio ( s ) Phoenix Pictures IndieProd Company Productions Silver Screen Partners Distributor Paramount Pictures Released February 17, 1984 Running time 110 minutes Language English Budget $ 8.2 million Source Footloose is a 1984 American musical drama film directed by Herbert Ross."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0266-37edbbfd3395:d01", "start": 525, "end": 674, "text": "It tells the story of Ren McCormack ( Kevin Bacon ), a teenager from Chicago who moves to a small town where dancing and rock music have been banned."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0266-37edbbfd3395:d01", "start": 675, "end": 799, "text": "The film features a hit soundtrack, including the main song performed by Taylor Swift, which became a chart-topping success."}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0266-37edbbfd3395:d02", "start": 0, "end": 212, "text": "Footloose (2011 soundtrack) Footloose: Music from the Motion Picture, the original soundtrack for the 2011 remake of \"Footloose\", was released by Atlantic Records and Warner Music Nashville on September 27, 2011."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0266-37edbbfd3395:d02", "start": 213, "end": 303, "text": "It includes eight new songs and four remakes of songs from the original film's soundtrack."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0266-37edbbfd3395:d02", "start": 304, "end": 413, "text": "\"Footloose\" by Kenny Loggins was covered by Blake Shelton for the remake, which is an upbeat country version."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0266-37edbbfd3395:d02", "start": 414, "end": 498, "text": "The film opens with several teens dancing to Loggins's original version of the song."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0266-37edbbfd3395:d02", "start": 499, "end": 624, "text": "Like the original film, the 2011 version also features \"Bang Your Head (Metal Health)\" by the heavy metal band Quiet Riot and"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0266-37edbbfd3395:d03", "start": 0, "end": 369, "text": "Footloose ( 2011 soundtrack ) - Wikipedia Home Random Nearby Log in Settings Donate About Wikipedia Disclaimers Search Footloose ( 2011 soundtrack ) Article Talk Language Watch Edit 